ng was involved in a controversial incident with Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/70178"} "Hanns Braun"] ".  On the first curve, Braun tried to cut in front of Young, who reacted by pushing Braun violently to the outside of the track.  Young finished first but was disqualified and Braun was advanced to the final, where he would compete against four Americans - Reidpath, Lindberg, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78784"} "Ted Meredith"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78493"} "Carroll Haff"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The first round and semi-finals had been run without lanes, but the Braun/Young incident changed that. Strings were put up for the final and the runners ran in lanes.  Braun took the lead until he was passed on the last curve by Reidpath.  Reidpath held on to narrowly defeat Braun, with Lindberg taking the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78935"} "Charles Reidpath"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "51.2 (2 h15)"] [:td {} "48.7 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "48.2 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/70178"} "Hanns Braun"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "50.6 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "49.2 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "48.3 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78701"} "Ed Lin